{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter10#prop:two-point-boundary-problem","title":"prop:two-point-boundary-problem","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter10.md","line":189,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter10.tex#prop:two-point-boundary-problem","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter10#prop:existence-uniqueness-jacobi-fields]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter10#cor:jacobi-field-tangent-vectors]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter10#prop:critical-points-conjugate]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter10.tex","label":"prop:two-point-boundary-problem","line":603,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[The Two-Point Boundary Value Theorem for Jacobi Fields]\n\\label{prop:two-point-boundary-problem}\n\\uses{prop:existence-uniqueness-jacobi-fields, cor:jacobi-field-tangent-vectors, prop:critical-points-conjugate}\n\\dcref{ch10:10.21}\n\n\nLet $(M,g)$ be Riemannian or pseudo-Riemannian and let\n$\\gamma:[a,b]\\to M$ be a geodesic segment. The two-point boundary problem\nhas a unique solution for every\n$v\\in T_{\\gamma(a)}M$ and $w\\in T_{\\gamma(b)}M$ if and only if\n$\\gamma(a)$ and $\\gamma(b)$ are not conjugate along $\\gamma$.\n\\end{proposition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[The Two-Point Boundary Value Theorem for Jacobi Fields] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a74776f2d706f696e742d626f756e646172792d70726f626c656d\"></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter10%23prop%3Aexistence-uniqueness-jacobi-fields\">↗ prop:existence-uniqueness-jacobi-fields</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter10%23cor%3Ajacobi-field-tangent-vectors\">↗ cor:jacobi-field-tangent-vectors</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter10%23prop%3Acritical-points-conjugate\">↗ prop:critical-points-conjugate</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch10:10.21</span></span><p></p>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> be Riemannian or pseudo-Riemannian and let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma :[a,b]\\to M$\">$\\gamma :[a,b]\\to M$</span> be a geodesic segment. The two-point boundary problem has a unique solution for every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v\\in T_{\\gamma (a)}M$\">$v\\in T_{\\gamma (a)}M$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$w\\in T_{\\gamma (b)}M$\">$w\\in T_{\\gamma (b)}M$</span> if and only if <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma (a)$\">$\\gamma (a)$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma (b)$\">$\\gamma (b)$</span> are not conjugate along <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma $\">$\\gamma $</span>. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter10#prop:critical-points-conjugate","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter10#thm:second-variation-formula","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter10#prop:existence-uniqueness-jacobi-fields","title":"prop:existence-uniqueness-jacobi-fields","label":"prop:existence-uniqueness-jacobi-fields"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter10#cor:jacobi-field-tangent-vectors","title":"cor:jacobi-field-tangent-vectors","label":"cor:jacobi-field-tangent-vectors"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter10#prop:critical-points-conjugate","title":"prop:critical-points-conjugate","label":"prop:critical-points-conjugate"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter10#prob:two-point-boundary-problem","title":"prob:two-point-boundary-problem","label":"prob:two-point-boundary-problem"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter10#prop:two-point-boundary-problem","title":"prop:two-point-boundary-problem","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[The Two-Point Boundary Value Theorem for Jacobi Fields]\n\\label{prop:two-point-boundary-problem}\n\\uses{prop:existence-uniqueness-jacobi-fields, cor:jacobi-field-tangent-vectors, prop:critical-points-conjugate}\n\\dcref{ch10:10.21}\n\n\nLet $(M,g)$ be Riemannian or pseudo-Riemannian and let\n$\\gamma:[a,b]\\to M$ be a geodesic segment. The two-point boundary problem\nhas a unique solution for every\n$v\\in T_{\\gamma(a)}M$ and $w\\in T_{\\gamma(b)}M$ if and only if\n$\\gamma(a)$ and $\\gamma(b)$ are not conjugate along $\\gamma$.\n\\end{proposition}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter10.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter10#prop:existence-uniqueness-jacobi-fields","title":"prop:existence-uniqueness-jacobi-fields","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter10#cor:jacobi-field-tangent-vectors","title":"cor:jacobi-field-tangent-vectors","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter10#prop:critical-points-conjugate","title":"prop:critical-points-conjugate","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}